{"id": "EUVD-2026-101870", "enisaUuid": "8227caf1-6508-351a-95fe-5c1c601c0df5", "description": "TLS 1.3 embeds the actual record type as the last non-zero byte of the decrypted payload, optionally followed by zero padding.  The code which searches for the inner record type had an off-by-one bug which could be triggered by an invalid frame, leading to an underflow followed by an unconditional NULL pointer dereference, causing a kernel panic.\n\nA remote TLS 1.3 peer can send a specially crafted record to trigger a kernel panic, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS).", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T06:53:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T13:55:00", "baseScore": 6.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://security.freebsd.org/advisories/FreeBSD-SA-26:67.ktls.asc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-101302"], "assigner": "freebsd", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3e913e29-c572-3444-9edd-1694f82d141f", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "14.4-RELEASE <p10"}, {"id": "479a821a-0c4b-32bc-8adc-177914976163", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "15.0-RELEASE <p14"}, {"id": "573bbe50-8650-3e94-9912-8edbe30f583d", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "15.1-RELEASE <p4"}, {"id": "ab310a36-08d0-3241-ab30-af489d01260c", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "14.5-RELEASE <p1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ec915c32-c013-38c0-8a26-f267a738927e", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}], "isExploited": false}